~ start
if not States.has_met_Hiro:
	set States.has_met_Hiro = true
	set States.has_talked_to_guard = true
	Guard: "Halt, Hiro. The council's mandate remains absolute—the outer perimeter is off-limits to all villagers."
	Hiro: "I'm not looking for trouble. I just need you to open the gate."
	Hiro: I just need that gate opened!
	Guard: "And violate protocol? Look around you, boy. That mountain isn't a gateway; it's a boundary meant to keep us alive."
else:
	% Guard: "Save your breath, Hiro. My standing orders haven't changed."
	% Guard: "Standing near the threshold won't make the iron yield, kid."
	% Guard: "Go back to the district before the elders notice you're missing."
	=> END

=> choices

~ choices

- "When does your watch shift officially end?"
	Guard: "My relief isn't bound by a clock. Protocol dictates I remain stationed here until the summit chime echoes through the valley."
	Hiro: "The summit chime?"
	Guard: "The ancient bronze bell perched on the eastern overlook. When it sounds, the morning guard takes over and I step down."
	=> END

- "Why is the village so terrified of what's beyond?"
	Guard: "Fear is what keeps this community intact. History proves that those who foolishly cross the threshold never return to tell the story."
	Guard: "Turn back, Hiro. Curiosity is a dangerous luxury."
	=> choices
	=> END